"""Lane B fixture harness: geppetto-live gate-launch / attach / receipt path.

FIXTURE ONLY. Never starts the real chest, never opens a real viewport,
never touches the real cabinet/confirm directory, never runs a paid
provider. Every subprocess runs with HOME pointed at a temp directory
containing a stub gate (see below), a stub host, a stub live_runs, a
stub receipt hook, and a fake runner.

GATE STUB DISCLOSURE: the fixture gate is tests/gate_stub_for_launcher_tests.py,
implementing the pre-Lane-A-change file/answer/claim/register surface
Lane B was built against at 03:36. The real gate.py in tree now requires
--worker/--session on claim (Lane A edit, 03:37, contract NOT yet
forwarded to Lane B), and the launcher must not guess how it obtains
those values. This harness therefore proves launcher logic (launch,
attach, receipt hook, cancel, trap, group kill), NOT integration against
Lane A's new claim signature. Re-point it at the real gate.py the moment
the coordinator forwards A's frozen contract.

The stub receipt hook RECORDS its invocation (run, answer, verb, token
presence); it does NOT validate a real receipt. Real build_execution
validation is covered by its own tests and by lane E integration.

Run:  python3 tests/test_gate_launcher_attach.py -v
from the project root on the PC. The launcher under test is
~/.local/bin/geppetto-live, copied into the fixture HOME.
"""

